<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Till-Abnu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1750 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Till-Abnu was a king of Apum in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> around 1750 BCE, ruling from Shehna, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-leilan">Tell Leilan</a>. He is known from the palace archives excavated there, which include a treaty he concluded with the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a>. His reign fell in the unsettled period after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamshi-adad-i">Shamshi-Adad I</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a> was rising.</p></div>
